alaux-bigmama-os
==========

A Copier template for BigMama (https://big-mama.io) NixOS machines.

It defines the operating system, packages and dotfiles shared across the
company's fleet. Generating from the template stamps out a configured host:
it sets the username, hostname, git identity, names the per-host folder and
regenerates the hardware configuration for the machine it runs on.


Bootstrap a new host
---------------------

Requires copier (it ships in the dev shell, or:
nix --extra-experimental-features 'nix-command flakes' shell nixpkgs#copier).

  copier copy --trust gh:bigmama/bigmama-nixos ./my-host
  # or from a local clone:
  copier copy --trust . ./my-host

You'll be asked for:

  username    system user account name
  hostname    machine hostname (also names the hosts/<hostname> folder)
  git_name    git user.name
  git_email   git user.email

--trust is required so the post-copy task can run nixos-generate-config and
write hosts/<hostname>/hardware-configuration.nix for THIS machine.

Then review and build:

  sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake .#<hostname>

Pull later template changes into an existing host:

  copier update --trust


Flake inputs
-------------

  nixpkgs          github:nixos/nixpkgs/nixos-26.05
  nixpkgs-unstable github:nixos/nixpkgs/nixos-unstable
  home-manager     github:nix-community/home-manager/release-26.05
  agents           github:numtide/llm-agents.nix   (opencode + claude-code)


Repo layout
------------

  base.nix               shared NixOS options (user, zsh, direnv, gc, nix-ld)
  flake.nix              flake with host outputs and dev shell
  flake.lock
  hosts/
    nixos/               primary workstation (x86_64-linux)
      configuration.nix  host-specific system packages and services
      home.nix           home-manager: GTK theme, systemd user services
      wayland.nix        niri / Hyprland / display-manager / font packages
      boot.nix           bootloader config
      networking.nix     network settings
      battery.nix        power management
      nvidia.nix         NVIDIA driver config
      virtualization.nix Docker / Podman
      hardware-configuration.nix
  modules/
    claude-code.nix      Claude Code agent service
    home/base.nix        shared home-manager base
    lid-screen.nix       lid-close screen handling
    systemd.nix          shared systemd tweaks
    tailscale.nix        Tailscale VPN
    virtualization.nix   container runtime options
  dotfiles/              GNU stow packages (stow --target=$HOME <pkg>)
    claude/              Claude Code config and projects
    direnv/              .envrc defaults
    eww/                 Eww bar widgets (todo, wifi, clock, etc.)
    hypr/                Hyprland config (secondary compositor)
    kitty/               kitty terminal config
    niri/                niri compositor config + keybindings
    quick-notes/         Quick Notes web app (Supabase-backed)
    television/          television fuzzy finder config
    zsh/                 .zshrc, aliases, starship prompt
  scripts/
    niri_toggle_window.sh  toggle/spawn a named niri floating window
  Taskfile.yml           task runner (go-task)


Host: nixos (alauxui's workstation)
-------------------------------------

Compositor     niri (Wayland, scrollable-tiling)
Browser        Brave
Terminal       kitty
Shell          zsh  (autosuggestions, syntax-highlighting, starship prompt)
Bar            eww  (left / right / bottom / middle panels)
Wallpaper      swaybg  (~/wallpaper.jpg, systemd user service)
GTK theme      Flat-Remix-GTK-Grey-Darkest
Night light    wlsunset  (Algiers coords, 36.75 N / 3.06 E)
Disks          udiskie  (automount, no tray icon)
Bluetooth      bluetui  (fast-connect, auto-enable on boot)
Keyboard       keyd  (CapsLock → Escape)
Mouse          piper / ratbagd
Screen lock    hyprlock
Audio          PipeWire + PulseAudio compat
AI             Claude Code + opencode  (via numtide/llm-agents.nix)

Key niri bindings
------------------

  Mod+T            kitty terminal
  Mod+N            Todo widget  (Brave app)
  Mod+Shift+N      Quick Notes  (Brave app, Supabase-synced)
  Mod+B            Brave browser
  Mod+D            App launcher  (tv cmds)
  Mod+F            Files picker  (tv files)
  Mod+E            yazi file manager
  Mod+P            Passwords  (pass + tv)
  Mod+I            Wi-Fi  (impala)
  Mod+Shift+B      Bluetooth  (bluetui)
  Mod+Shift+O      opencode session picker
  Mod+Shift+C      Clipboard history
  Mod+Slash        Show current time  (notify-send)
  Mod+Shift+Slash  Hotkey overlay


Quick Notes
------------

A minimal notes app that syncs to Supabase. Opens in a standalone Brave
window (no browser chrome) via the Mod+Shift+N keybinding or the app launcher.

  dotfiles/quick-notes/.local/share/quick-notes/index.html
  dotfiles/quick-notes/.local/share/applications/quick-notes.desktop

Supabase project: pvztksawvnyeaylkxxrz.supabase.co
Required table (run once in the SQL editor):

  create table notes (
    id         text        primary key,
    title      text        not null default '',
    body       text        not null default '',
    created_at timestamptz not null default now(),
    updated_at timestamptz not null default now()
  );
  alter table notes enable row level security;
  create policy "allow all for anon" on notes for all using (true) with check (true);


Dotfiles workflow
------------------

Dotfiles live under dotfiles/ and are symlinked into $HOME with GNU stow.
To apply a package on a new machine:

  cd ~/nixos/dotfiles && stow --target=$HOME <package>

All packages are already stowed on the current machine.


Dev shell
----------

  nix develop   # provides go-task, stow, pre-commit, copier


